The focal-point detection feature unconditionally added `img.crossOrigin = "anonymous"` to image loading. When image servers don't return CORS headers, the browser blocks the image entirely — killing all background image functionality.

### Changes

- **Conditional CORS**: Only set `crossOrigin = "anonymous"` when `FaceDetector` API is available (the only feature requiring it)
- **Fallback on CORS failure**: Added `onerror` handler that retries without `crossOrigin` so images still load even when servers reject CORS
- **Extract `applyLoadedImage()` helper**: Consolidates the image→state logic used by both primary and fallback paths

```typescript
if (faceDetector) {
  img.crossOrigin = "anonymous";
}
img.onload = () => { applyLoadedImage(img, !!faceDetector && !!img.crossOrigin, onLoaded); };
img.onerror = () => {
  if (!img.crossOrigin) return;
  // CORS rejected — retry without crossOrigin
  const fallback = new Image();
  fallback.onload = () => { applyLoadedImage(fallback, false, onLoaded); };
  fallback.src = url;
};
```
